From 68b586653e32fa26aba1222fc2fbeef9991169e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:58:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add DVD multi-view stereo layers

A design layer can be marked as a stereo layer: each view is written with
its own scrambled-byte sequence whose EFMPlus marks form a nearly pure
along-track grating (5F C5DB F9 CC67 6F DDB6 A5, 2.13-0.85 um), so each
view leaves at its own diffraction angle and moving the head along the
track switches views, lenticular-card style.

- StereoOverlay (DvdImageSolver): per-codeword override loaded from a
  <picture>.stereo.json sidecar, so ISO export, stream burn and the CLI
  all apply it; explicit 2-7 view images or one image plus a depth map;
  interleave cell length, copies round the disc, reverse order.
- Blocks touching a stereo layer use the scalar sampler; all others keep
  SIMD and sample reuse. Output is byte-identical to a direct
  per-codeword reference.
- Project schema: optional ProjectLayer.Stereo, validated.
- Design page: stereo controls in the layer properties, faded copies on
  the canvas, copies in composites, 'point outward' helper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxNFJdceW8VtXpKpEJ6Ejb
